# Both spellings, deliberately. A trailing slash matches a directory only, so a
# *symlink* named node_modules walked straight past this rule and was committed
# — pointing at an absolute path on one machine, which is a dangling link in
# anybody else's clone and a self-referential one in the machine that made it.
node_modules/
node_modules
out/
dist/
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
relay/dist/
